  "analysis": "C3 (§10.3) reports three cycles and one incompatible order. G-nonadjacent: cycle i=3214 -rw(k=9)-> i=3226 -ww(k=9)-> i=3230 -rw(k=13)-> i=3178 -wr(k=12)-> i=3214. G-single: cycle i=3230 -rw(k=13)-> i=3178 -ww(k=12)-> i=3230. G2-item: cycle i=3214 -rw(k=12)-> i=3230 -rw(k=13)-> i=3178 -wr(k=12)-> i=3214. incompatible-order on key 14: value 48, appended by the info transaction i=3093, read by ok i=3214 and absent from the key's longest read (ok i=3813). Every cycle runs through i=3178, a transaction whose completion is info (invoked 20.227 s, client P01 deadline at 30.227 s, §6.2 row 9); the other transactions the cycles name are ok. Faults (all F1c): the leader n1 cut off from orchestrators, followers and etcd but not from the gateways at 10.442–41.992 s; n3 became primary at 35.26 s (rule 2.0); n1 did not rejoin before the run ended; F1c on n3 at 55.483–87.030 s and 101.172–112.734 s without a leader change. i=3214 (ok, 31.185 s, gw-z2) read key 12 ending in 62, the element i=3178 appended; the final reads of key 12 end in 58 64, without 62. C3 infers key 12's version order from the transactions' reads, not from final reads (LIM-22), so that order contains 62, a value the failover removed; the edges ww(k=12) and wr(k=12) through i=3178 come from it. ADR-0045: the incompatible-order group matches R-G2b (the vanish of FND-D1-fb8d0f8c, FND-D1-2e860fd2, FND-D1-a8eb9857, FND-C2-2a534585); the cycle classes are groups of their own, which match no predicate, so the run is a new failure. Minimization (§12.2): 11 candidates, none showed G-nonadjacent; the minimized plan is the original's. P13 replays of it: 0 of 5 show G-nonadjacent; all 5 are FAIL with incompatible-order only (a further attempt was INVALID, recovery deadline P06 exceeded, NOTES §7, and was re-run with the same plan). Oracle (ADR-0046): oracle-disagreement. elle-cli agrees on validity (false), on incompatible-order and on the same G-single through keys 12 and 13; its cycle search timed out and gave no answer for G-nonadjacent and G2-item, which are not confirmed. Hypothesis, not shown: the cycles are the vanish's effect on the inferred version order (a commit locally visible after a cancelled synchronous-replication wait, S61, then removed by the failover, LIM-33) rather than an isolation anomaly of their own. The replays reproduced the vanish without the cycles; origin UNDETERMINED.",
